  "description": "Replace 4x single-glazed wooden sash windows with double-glazed wood-grain effect uPVC sash windows. The replacements are period style in keeping with the character of the property. The windows to be replaced are two at the front of the property (living room) facing onto Willow Vale, one in the bedroom facing the back garden, and one in the bathroom facing the back garden. All four windows are on the ground floor. The glass of the new bathroom window will have a stained glass decorative pattern, the remaining three replacement windows will have clear glass. Prior to the replacement, the bedroom and bathroom windows had glazing bars; after the replacement, all four windows will not have glazing bars. The new windows will match the existing window openings in size and position.\n\nThe replacement windows are to be \"Legacy\" brand with white woodgrain Effect, with tilt-back mechanism, run-through horns, and magnetic restrictors. Accessories such as the window locks will be gold in colour. The windows will have trickle vents and safety-toughened glass on the lower sections to meet FENSA requirements. The uPVC wood-grain effect finish will closely replicate the appearance of painted timber. All work will be carried out from within the property's boundaries. All waste will be disposed of responsibly. The new double-glazed units will improve the property's energy efficiency and replace unsightly rotten timber while preserving its character.",
  "subdivision_of_building": "The proposal affects the ground floor (112 Willow Vale) only. The upper floor (114 Willow Vale) is unaffected.",
